  "keywords": [
    "publisher-tested"
  ],
  "ingredients": [
    "6 bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs",
    "kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste",
    "8 ounces bacon, sliced crosswise into 1/2-inch pieces",
    "10 large button mushrooms, quartered",
    "0.5 large yellow onion, diced",
    "2 shallots, sliced",
    "2 teaspoons all-purpose flour",
    "2 teaspoons butter",
    "1.5 cups red wine",
    "6 sprigs fresh thyme",
    "1 cup chicken broth"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Season chicken thighs all over with salt and black pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/8MIx_SaUzRijjvOXxBSursWtzBA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step1_4x3_0933-d9ad732ff33b4ca49c2df2ecb46ebaa9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook bacon in a large, oven-proof skillet over medium-high heat, turning occasionally, until evenly browned, about 10 minutes. Transfer bacon to a paper towel-lined plate, using a slotted spoon, leaving drippings in the skillet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/lAg1J6foNnPGKxpSnlrUGv-7aL8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step2_4x3_0939-d298cfc7ae0344b7b43d6a4522049e2a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increase the heat to high; place chicken thighs, skin-sides down, into the skillet. Cook until browned, 2 to 4 minutes per side. Transfer chicken to a plate; drain and discard all but 1 tablespoon drippings from the skillet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IZtnE694OB3oDqmKTCe-mKFfwt8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step3_4x3_0947-86c0f61ef56e4a76a92764e7e6c4e6ad.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce the heat to medium-high. Add mushrooms, onion, and shallots with a pinch of salt to the skillet; cook until golden and caramelized, 7 to 12 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/6PxtRj6I-g4b1gayvOp190wDTQ4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step4_4x3_0948-f8093a03afac4b488d1a939211d5d337.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir flour and butter into mushroom mixture until completely incorporated, about 1 minute.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/T_HPe8-Dr20r3Iqh8ngANetzeIA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step5_4x3_0951-c30c330dd29b461482f2aa115e70931d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour red wine into the skillet and bring to a boil while scraping the browned bits of food off of the bottom of the skillet with a wooden spoon. Stir in bacon and thyme; simmer until wine is reduced by about ⅓, 3 to 5 minutes. Add chicken broth; return chicken thighs to the skillet and bring to a simmer.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7E1fN26RoWlI_pdsY1azyumbVX4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step6_4x3_0964-e2199aeb064a47e0ab756d56412e0c74.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer the skillet to the preheated oven; cook for 30 minutes. Spoon skillet juices over chicken; continue cooking until chicken is no longer pink at the bone and the juices run clear, about 30 minutes more. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the thigh, near not but not touching the bone should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Transfer chicken to a platter.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/cYXPC9BZdr6omhdoZ2RcxwAmxtk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230_ChefJohnsCoqAuVin_ddmfs_step7_4x3_09640990-957776c718624504a11945412d74bad3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the skillet over high heat; reduce skillet juices, skimming fat off top as necessary, until sauce thickens slightly, about 5 minutes. Season with salt and black pepper; remove and discard thyme. Pour sauce over chicken to serve.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Q61_c1qE1D9o1wk0fpy8vd-EzPc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/239230-chef-johns-coq-au-vin-MFS_364-357b537b2e324407b6559d6cc33e5738.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/239230/step_08.webp"
    }
  ],
